  "abstract": "GenSfM reconstructs complete object geometry, appearance, and camera poses from a few uncalibrated images. A native 3D diffusion transformer jointly denoises shared shape and compact per-view pose latents. A pose-aware refinement stage uses image features to recover geometry and texture, without an external pose estimator or post-hoc optimization. Four-view evaluations on Toys4K and GSO show improved reconstruction fidelity and camera recovery over the compared baselines.",
  "contributions": [
    {
      "title": "Joint shape and camera reasoning",
      "description": "A shared diffusion transformer jointly recovers object structure and camera poses, completing surfaces hidden from the inputs."
    },
    {
      "title": "Compact, 3D-native pose tokens",
      "description": "Each view uses a compact 4 × 4 × 4 pose latent that communicates with the shared shape."
    },
    {
      "title": "Pose-aware detail and texture",
      "description": "Recovered cameras align semantic and texture features with active voxels to refine geometry and appearance."
    }
  ],
  "method": {
    "image": "assets/derived/pipeline-dlt.webp",
    "alt": "GenSfM coarse-to-fine pipeline with a joint shape-pose diffusion transformer and pose-aware fine generation.",
    "caption": "Joint shape-and-pose diffusion recovers structure and cameras; pose-aligned image features then refine geometry and appearance."
  },
